I can't recall any specific occurrences, but I have many times preferred
the second rated lujvo to the first rated one, and each time it was because
I liked the vowel ending leading rafsi version better than the consonant
ending leading rafsi that got the highest score.

Perhaps a change to the algorithm should be made to give preference to
vowel ending rafsi?

